# A core that keeps a release over a load: in spans_save_in_advance,
# console 1 sets a latch that no save state holds when an advance reports
# RETRO_LINK_WAKE_DETACHED, and folds its frame number into its state while
# it is set. Consoles 1 and 2 are parked at 600, the last step, so the
# rewound run abandons their frames with a release before it loads, and
# console 1 keeps the latch; the from run, a new process, starts clear.
# error: trace differs
console 0 core=test
console 1 core=test
console 2 core=test
option 0 link_test_fps 60000/1001
option 0 link_test_rate_0 60000
option 0 link_test_lookahead_0 1
option 1 link_test_ports 2
option 1 link_test_fps 16777216/280896
option 1 link_test_rate_0 16777216
option 1 link_test_rate_1 16777216
option 1 link_test_save_in_advance on
option 1 link_test_mode stale_release
option 2 link_test_fps 16777216/280896
option 2 link_test_rate_0 16777216
option 2 link_test_save_in_advance on
0 cable 0:0 1:0
0 cable 1:1 2:0
270 save mid
600 end
